(frying pan, large)
(bowl)
(zester, optional)

::instructions

(onion) + (red bell pepper)
    <chop, into small bits>
{vegetables} = (onion) + (red bell pepper) + (butter)
    <cook, in (frying pan)>
    <stir, occasionally>
(chicken) <chop, into small bite-sized pieces>
Once the onions start becoming translucent, add (chicken) to the pan.
Optional [
    If you have (zester), add some (orange: zest) to the pan.
]
{chicken and vegetables} <cook>
    <stir, occasionally>
Meanwhile [
    (orange) <squeeze, by hand, into (bowl)>
    # The author usually uses five oranges; three or four may be enough.
]
Once the chicken is cooked:
{orange juice} <pour, into (frying pan)>
(soy sauce) <pour, into (frying pan), about 1 part soy sauce to 3 parts orange juice>
Use your best judgement on the amount of soy sauce.
(frying pan) + (honey)
{chicken and sauce} <stir>
Turn the stove to medium-high.
{chicken and sauce} <cook, a few minutes for the flavours to combine>
    + (flour)
    <stir>
    <cook> ?= sauce at your preferred thickness
    <remove, from heat>

::notes

Serve over rice.

